{"name":"Bella Mia","hex":"#dac5bd","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mia","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Miami."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An ancient bluffing game played with dice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bella","blocks":[{"text":"Bella is a feminine given name. It is a diminutive or nickname form of names ending in -bella, including Izabella and Isabella. However, it can also derive, unrelatedly, from the Italian, Spanish, Portuguese and (ultimately) Latin words for \"beautiful\". In French, Belle is a name and word meaning beautiful."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bella","wikidata":"Q792453"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"mia":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/En-au-mia.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/90/En-au-mia.ogg/En-au-mia.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Bella mia - chanson vénitienne - poésie de Léon Durocher ; musique de Paul Fauchey - bpt6k1177283g (2 of 2)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Bella_mia_-_chanson_v%C3%A9nitienne_-_po%C3%A9sie_de_L%C3%A9on_Durocher_%3B_musique_de_Paul_Fauchey_-_bpt6k1177283g_%282_of_2%29.jpg/500px-Bella_mia_-_chanson_v%C3%A9nitienne_-_po%C3%A9sie_de_L%C3%A9on_Durocher_%3B_musique_de_Paul_Fauchey_-_bpt6k1177283g_%282_of_2%29.jpg","ratio":1.2714798395609035,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bella_mia_-_chanson_v%C3%A9nitienne_-_po%C3%A9sie_de_L%C3%A9on_Durocher_;_musique_de_Paul_Fauchey_-_bpt6k1177283g_(2_of_2).jpg","share":0.683125},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w